{"resourceIdentifier":"2879","resourceName":"Henan Lehuijia Composting Project","description":"The project introduced a set of organic fertilizers production lines with an annual output of 30,000 tons to treat the manure from the chicken farms and Biomass waste residue i.e., straw in Gushi county, Xinyang city, Henan Province. The purpose of the project activity is to avoid methane emissions through controlled aerobic treatment by composting of manure and biomass residue.\r\nIn absence of the project, all manure waste produced was left to decay in uncovered anaerobic lagoons, which is the most economic, viable and reasonable for livestock farm owners and the biomass waste residue had been left to decay anaerobically in a solid waste disposal site (SWDS).\r\nThe proposed project was designed to treat the chicken manure and biomass waste residue- straw in Gushi county to produce organic fertilizer. The proposed project comprises of fermentation system and fertilizer production system, etc. It is estimated that approximately 56,250 tons of manure and 18,750 tons of biomass waste residue can treat annually, therefore total 75,000 tons of waste can be composted aerobically every year for this project. The final compost obtained will be sold to local businesses. The construction start date of the project is 01/08/2020 and was put into operation on 15/10/2020.\r\nThe project activity will reduce of GHG in the atmosphere through avoiding methane emissions from controlled aerobic treatment by composting of manure and biomass residue. It is estimated that 40,091 tCO2e emission reductions will be generated annually and total emission reductions are 400,913 tCO2e in the 10 years’ fixing crediting period.","location":{"latitude":31.984860,"longitude":115.680694},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-03-17","endExclusive":"2022-04-17","endInclusive":"2022-04-16"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2879"